Roast.pet Frontier Stack =E2=80=94 1 useful find Realtime-Venus (inclusionA=
I / Ant
Group + Tsinghua) =E2=80=94 TEST

Source: https://huggingface.co/inclusionAI/Realtime-Venus
Release: 2026-09-16 (fresh open-weight release; technical report
arXiv:2609.13814)

WHAT CHANGED
A genuinely open, Apache-2.0, 9B full-duplex multimodal interaction stack
has appeared with downloadable weights and runnable code. There are two
checkpoints: Realtime-Venus-Omni (video/images + audio + text =E2=86=92 tex=
t +
speech) and Realtime-Venus-Audio (audio + text =E2=86=92 text + speech). Un=
like
ordinary STT=E2=86=92LLM=E2=86=92TTS pipelines, it keeps perceiving while s=
peaking,
distinguishes backchannels/interruption/correction/redirection, can
proactively respond to audiovisual events, and emits asynchronous requests
to a companion harness without blocking the live conversation.

ROAST.PET CAPABILITY
This is specifically interesting for the QR/AR V2: a pet can continuously
watch/listen to its owner, interrupt naturally, react to something
happening on camera, and delegate a harder roast/retrieval task while
conversation continues. More importantly, it offers a self-hosted
alternative to GPT-Live/Grok Voice/Murf-style cloud voice infrastructure,
making PetPersona portable.

INPUTS / OUTPUTS
Omni: streaming video/images + 16kHz-class audio + text =E2=86=92 text + na=
tive
speech. Audio checkpoint: audio + text =E2=86=92 text + native speech. Cont=
ext:
40,960 tokens. Speech uses discrete S3 tokens plus a streaming
flow-matching decoder.

INSTALL / API ROUTE
No hosted inference provider is currently listed. Download from Hugging
Face (inclusionAI/Realtime-Venus) and run with Python 3.10 + CUDA + FFmpeg
via Hugging Face Transformers/custom code. The companion Realtime-Venus
Harness provides asynchronous delegation/tool integration.

PRICING
Weights/code: $0. Infrastructure cost only. No serverless/API price exists
yet.

COMMERCIAL LICENSE
Apache-2.0 according to the official Hugging Face model card. This is
materially cleaner for commercial experimentation than several recent
video-model community licenses.

PRIVACY / SELF-HOSTING
Strong: downloadable weights and local inference mean customer
conversational audio/video can remain inside Roast.pet infrastructure. This
is the main reason it clears the scanner threshold despite not being part
of V1.

QUALITY / LATENCY CONSTRAINTS
Very early release. Both checkpoints are 9B BF16; the distributed files are
large and practical GPU memory is substantial. No mature hosted endpoint or
production SLA. The authors report full-duplex/interruption benchmarks, but
Roast.pet still needs a real conversational test because pet-comedy timing
is not a benchmark target. The Omni path also does not itself animate the
canonical pet image; it is the conversational brain/voice layer, not the
avatar renderer.

EXACT ROAST.PET USE CASE
QR on card/T-shirt =E2=86=92 browser camera/mic =E2=86=92 Realtime-Venus se=
ssion seeded
with PetPersona/customer facts =E2=86=92 pet notices owner/environment,
interrupts/reacts/roasts =E2=86=92 optional avatar renderer drives the pet =
visual.
Keep the fixed V1 video path unchanged.

SMALLEST TEST
Do not integrate AR/video first. Rent a suitable GPU for one hour and run
Realtime-Venus-Audio with one PetPersona. Perform 20 scripted two-minute
sessions containing interruptions, backchannels, corrections and delayed
punchlines. Compare against GPT-Live/Grok/Murf on: first-audio latency,
interruption correctness, punchlines/minute, controllability, voice
quality, VRAM and actual $/session. Only test Omni camera input if Audio
wins.

DECISION: TEST =E2=80=94 not ADOPT. It is too early for production, but it =
is the
first recent open stack that materially changes the ownership/privacy
economics of the interactive-pet path.
TOP 5 STACK CHANGES TO TEST NOW

   1. Realtime-Venus-Audio vs hosted live-voice providers for the future
   PetPersona/QR path.
   2. H3 Max vs LongCat vs Wan on the fixed hard-pet lip-sync corpus.
   3. P-Video-2-Pro Speed for cheap best-of-N draft motion.
   4. Local PetPrep =E2=86=92 fur/edge QC =E2=86=92 hosted fallback.
   5. Multi-take TTS =E2=86=92 comedy ranking =E2=86=92 animate only winner=
 =E2=86=92 AV-QC/retry.

CHEAPEST MEANINGFUL CAPABILITY IMPROVEMENT

PetPrep/local segmentation remains effectively $0 marginal inference.
Realtime-Venus is also $0 software/model cost, but requires GPU compute, so
it is not automatically cheaper than hosted live voice at low volume.
BIGGEST CAPABILITY SHOCK THIS HOUR

Not a new image/video generator: a genuinely downloadable Apache-2.0
full-duplex audiovisual model now makes a private/self-hosted interactive
Roast.pet technically plausible without building STT=E2=86=92LLM=E2=86=92TT=
S orchestration
ourselves.
CONCRETE STACK SIMPLIFICATION

Formalize one LivePetBrain interface now, but do not build the UI around
any provider:
PetPersona + live audio/video =E2=86=92 LivePetBrain =E2=86=92 response aud=
io/text +
events/delegations.
Backends can then be RealtimeVenus | GPT-Live | Grok | Murf. The visual pet
renderer remains downstream and independent.

No other sufficiently fresh, verified Roast.pet-specific release cleared
the bar this run; mature unchanged tools and marketing-only launches were
excluded.

